binary comparison: a strong tournament with two disjoint cycles has order >= 6, so alpha_1 >= 6 (Moon) and
  alpha_2 >= 1, and its binary alpha-sum alpha_1 + 2 alpha_2 + ... is >= 8; hence for a <= 7 every strong
